  "final_message": "I haven't made any changes. The repo shows that something does still read `channel`.\n\n`contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` is the deployed contract (`deployedVersion: 3`) for the analytics-ingest service. It lists `channel` (`enum:web|store|marketplace`) as a required field on `OrderPlaced`. If I remove it from the event, `npm run contracts` (`scripts/verify-contracts.mjs`, the ARCH-4 event-contract check) will fail. More importantly, analytics-ingest could break in production when it gets events without the field.\n\nThe field also matters inside this service. `channel` is required on `POST /orders` (`src/api/requestParsing.ts:18`) and checked in `src/core/order.ts:124`, so removing it from the order model also changes the public request format. CLAUDE.md, the README and the contract script's sample order all send it.\n\nHow do you want to go ahead?\n\n1. **Coordinate first (recommended):** check with the analytics-ingest owners whether they still use `channel`. If they don't, they publish a new contract version without it, and then I remove it here along with the contract file entry.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only:** keep `channel` on `OrderPlaced` and the request so analytics-ingest keeps working. This doesn't save much, because the event needs the value from somewhere.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now:** I'd also update the analytics-ingest contract file. That would make the check pass, but it would only hide the break, so I'd only do it if you've confirmed with that team that they no longer read the field.\n\nIf you already know the contract is out of date, tell me and I'll do option 3, including the tests, docs and the script's sample order.",
